node_modules/
dist/
webview/dist/
*.vsix
.vscode-test/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Full copy of the ghost.one project, kept in-tree on purpose as a quality
# reference. Never committed here (it has its own repo) and never packed into
# a VSIX — 3.8 GB that vsce would otherwise walk on every package.
ghost.one/

# The toolchain is bun: bun.lock IS tracked. npm lockfiles are not — if one
# reappears, something ran npm install and the two would drift apart.
package-lock.json
webview/package-lock.json

# Working notes, kept local on purpose — written for us, not for a reader of the
# repo. PLAN.md is the phase log, DESIGN.md the rationale behind decisions already
# made, and TESTING.md a point-in-time coverage report carrying a known-issues
# list, which reads as current documentation and is not.
#
# `docs/TOKENS.md` is deliberately NOT here: it is the contract a theme has to
# satisfy, seven files in `webview/src/` point a reader at it, and anyone touching
# the UI needs it.
docs/PLAN.md
docs/DESIGN.md
TESTING.md

# The parity work's own notes. These quote a proprietary bundle at length —
# paths, sizes, argv, wire protocol, read out of a shipped artefact for our own
# use. Describing a competitor's internals is a working method, not a document
# to publish under this repository's name. The audits directory is otherwise
# committed on purpose; this one file is the exception, not a new rule.
docs/PARITY-PLAN.md
docs/WORKFLOW-AGENTS-PANEL.md
.claude/audits/parity-vs-official-and-cli.md

# Personal workspace preferences — `luno.permissionMode: auto` in particular has
# no business being a default for anyone who clones this. `launch.json` and
# `tasks.json` stay: those are the dev loop, and they are the same for everyone.
.vscode/settings.json

# The agent environment IS committed — CLAUDE.md, rules, hooks, skills and the
# shared permission list are project tooling and belong with the project. Only
# the per-machine layer stays out: `settings.local.json` accumulates a personal
# allow-list, and the codex-threads directory is scratch state.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/codex-threads/

# Playwright MCP scratch — screenshots and console logs from the harness.
.playwright-mcp/
.luno/

# Scratch from probe agents reading the CLI binary.
.tmp-cli-probe/

# Live probes and throwaway scripts — re-runnable, never shipped.
external/scratch/

# Recorders downloaded from a CI run to test a package locally. Built by
# `.github/workflows/native.yml` for every release and never committed: a
# binary in git is one nobody can prove came from the source beside it.
external/audio/
